WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.658
Two vaults can hold the same thousand sources.

00:00:03.758 --> 00:00:08.828
One is a research partner. One is an unsearchable pile.

00:00:08.878 --> 00:00:11.252
The difference is entirely in the rules.

00:00:12.452 --> 00:00:14.790
A page holds one idea.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:19.375
One covering four topics drags three irrelevant ones into context.

00:00:19.425 --> 00:00:23.906
One idea is linked precisely, and updated without collateral damage.

00:00:24.456 --> 00:00:33.534
Every page declares one of four types. Sources, entities, concepts, which compound,

00:00:33.584 --> 00:00:36.630
and synthesis, only when it says something no single source did.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.157
Links are the entire value of the structure.

00:00:40.207 --> 00:00:44.842
Link the first mention of any concept or entity, on every page.

00:00:45.392 --> 00:00:51.227
When a new source disagrees, the page records both. Each with its source and date,

00:00:51.277 --> 00:00:52.574
and what would settle it.

00:00:53.124 --> 00:00:58.811
Last, two files that are not knowledge. The index, a catalog.

00:00:58.861 --> 00:01:03.426
The log, one line per operation. Both update in the same run.

00:01:03.976 --> 00:01:09.958
That's chapter four, structuring. Start with page one: One page, one idea.
